#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:60
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:62
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwrite; is more than a text editor for the &kde; Desktop. It is meant to be "
"a programmer's editor, and could be considered as at least a partial "
"alternative to more powerful editors. It may be best used in conjunction "
"with &konqueror; or &dolphin; for source file browsing for different "
"languages. &kwrite; also works very well as a simple text editor. One of "
"&kwrite;'s main features is the colorized syntax, customized for many "
"different programming languages such as: C/C++, &Java;, Python, Perl, Bash, "
"Modula 2, &HTML;, and Ada."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwrite; has a single document interface (<acronym>SDI</acronym>) allowing "
"you to edit one file at the time per window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; features two different modes, a simple mode with a "
"straightforward interface and an advanced mode with more features and more "
"extensive menu items. The advanced mode is enabled by checking the option "
"<link linkend=\"appearance\"> Enable Power User Mode (&kde; 3 mode)</link> "
"on the <guilabel>Appearance</guilabel> page in &kappname;s settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:86
#, no-c-format
msgid "Some Fundamentals"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:88
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwrite; is very simple to use. Anyone that has used a text editor should "
"have no problems."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid "Drag and Drop"
msgstr "Rossegar e pausar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kwrite; uses the &kde; Drag and Drop protocol. Files may be dragged and "
"dropped onto &kwrite; from the Desktop, the filemanager &dolphin;, or some "
"remote &FTP; site opened in one of &dolphin;'s windows."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "Command Line Options"
msgstr "Opcions de linha de comanda"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Though &kwrite; may most often be started from the &kde; program menu, or a "
"desktop icon, it can also be opened at the command line prompt of a terminal "
"window. There are a few useful options that are available when doing this."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid "Specify a File"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"By specifying the path and name of a particular file the user can have "
"&kwrite; open (or create) that file immediately upon startup. This option "
"might look something like the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>kwrite</command>\n"
"<option><replaceable>/home/myhome/docs/myfile.txt</replaceable></option>\n"
"</userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:124
#, no-c-format
msgid "Specify a file on the internet"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:126
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The above-mentioned method could even be used to open files on the internet "
"(if the user has an active connection at the time.) An example of this might "
"look like the following:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screen
#: index.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>kwrite</command>\n"
"<option><replaceable>ftp://ftp.kde.org/pub/kde/README</replaceable>\n"
"</option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid "Other Command Line Options"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid "The following command line help options are available"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:142
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>--help</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:144
#, no-c-format
msgid "This lists the most basic options available at the command line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:148
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>--help-qt</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:150
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This lists the options available for changing the way &kwrite; interacts "
"with &Qt;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:154
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>--help-kde</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This lists the options available for changing the way &kwrite; interacts "
"with &kde;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>--help-all</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:162
#, no-c-format
msgid "This lists all of the command line options."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:165
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>--author</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:167
#, no-c-format
msgid "Lists &kwrite;'s authors in the terminal window"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:171
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>-v, --version</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:173
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Lists version information for &Qt;, &kde;, and &kwrite;. Also available "
"through <userinput><command>kwrite</command> <option>-v</option></userinput>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:178
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>&kwrite;</command> <option>--license</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:181
#, no-c-format
msgid "Shows license information."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid "<command>kwrite</command> <option>--stdin</option>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Causes &kwrite; to read the document content from STDIN. This is similar to "
"the common option <option>-</option> used in many command line programs, and "
"allows you to pipe command output into &kwrite;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kwrite</command> <option>--encoding</option> <parameter>encoding</"
"parameter> <parameter>&URL;</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:195
#, no-c-format
msgid "Causes &kwrite; to use the specified encoding for the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:199
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kwrite</command> <option>--line</option> <parameter>line</"
"parameter> <parameter>&URL;</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:202
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigate to the specified line after opening the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: userinput
#: index.docbook:206
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<command>kwrite</command> <option>--column</option> <parameter>column</"
"parameter> <parameter>&URL;</parameter>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid "Navigate to the specified column after opening the document."
msgstr ""

