#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:544
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Menu Entries"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:546
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"There are different menus and menu items in simple and advanced mode. The "
"advanced mode is enabled by checking the option <link linkend=\"appearance"
"\"> Enable Power User Mode (&kde; 3 mode)</link> on the "
"<guilabel>Appearance</guilabel> page in &kappname;s settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>File</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:565
#, no-c-format
msgid "This starts a new document in a new and independent editor window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:573
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>O</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Open...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:624
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Displays a standard &kde; <guilabel>Open File</guilabel> dialog. Use the "
"file view to select the file you want to open, and click on <guibutton>Open</"
"guibutton> to open it. You can find more information about the &kde; "
"<guilabel>Open File</guilabel> dialog in the &kde; User Guide."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:635
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Open Recent</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:641
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a shortcut to open recently saved documents. Clicking on this item "
"opens a list to the side of the menu with several of the most recently saved "
"files. Clicking on a specific file will open it in &kappname; - if the file "
"still resides at the same location."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:653
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>S</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Save</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:662
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This saves the current document. If there has already been a save of the "
"document then this will overwrite the previously saved file without asking "
"for the user's consent. If it is the first save of a new document the save "
"as dialog (described below) will be invoked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:673
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Save As...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:679
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This allows a document to be saved with a new file name. This is done by "
"means of the file dialog box described above in the <link linkend=\"open"
"\">Open</link> section of this help file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:689
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F5</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Reload</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:698
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Reloads the active file from disk. This command is useful if another program "
"or process has changed the file while you have it open in &kappname;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:707
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Print...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:716
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Opens a simple print dialog allowing the user to specify what, where, and "
"how to print."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:724
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Export as HTML...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:730
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Export your file in &HTML; format so your document can be viewed as a web "
"page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:737
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>W</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Close</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:746
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Close the active file with this command. If you have made unsaved changes, "
"you will be prompted to save the file before &kappname; closes it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:755
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:764
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will close the editor window, if you have more than one instance of "
"&kappname; running, through the <guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem> or "
"<guimenuitem>New Window</guimenuitem> menu items, those instances will not "
"be closed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:778
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:782
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Z</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Undo</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:788
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is used to eliminate or reverse the most recent user action or "
"operation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:800
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>Z</keycap></"
"keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Redo</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:805
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will reverse the most recent change (if any) made using Undo"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:810
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>X</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Cut</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:815
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This command deletes the current selection and places it on the clipboard. "
"The clipboard is a feature of &kde; that works invisibly to provide a way to "
"transfer data between applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:823
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Copy</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:828
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This copies the currently selected text to the clipboard so that it may be "
"pasted elsewhere. The clipboard is a feature of &kde; that works invisibly "
"to provide a way to transfer data between applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:834
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Copy as HTML...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:838
#, no-c-format
msgid "This copies the currently selected text to the clipboard as &HTML;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:842
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>V</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Paste</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:847
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will insert the contents of the clipboard at the cursor position. The "
"clipboard is feature of &kde; that works invisibly to provide a way to "
"transfer data between applications."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:854
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>A</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Select All</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:859
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will select the entire document. This could be very useful for copying "
"the entire file to another application."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:865
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>A</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Deselect</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:871
#, no-c-format
msgid "Deselects the selected text in the editor if any."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:875
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>B</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Block Selection "
"Mode</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:882
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Toggles Selection Mode. When the Selection Mode is <guilabel>BLOCK</"
"guilabel>, you can make vertical selections, &eg; select column 5 to 10 in "
"lines 9 to 15. The status bar shows the current state of the Selection Mode, "
"either <guilabel>BLOCK</guilabel> or <guilabel>LINE</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:889
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>Ins</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Overwrite Mode</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:896
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Toggles the Insert/Overwrite modes. When the mode is <guilabel>INS</"
"guilabel>, you insert characters where the cursor is. When the mode is "
"<guilabel>OVR</guilabel>, writing characters will replace the current "
"characters if your cursor is positioned before any character. The status bar "
"shows the current state of the Overwrite Mode, either <guilabel>INS</"
"guilabel> or <guilabel>OVR</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:905
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Find...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:910
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This opens the incremental search bar at the bottom of the editor window. On "
"the left side of the bar is an icon to close the bar, followed by a small "
"text box for entering the search pattern."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:913
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you start entering characters of your search pattern, the search starts "
"immediately. If there is a match in the text this is highlighted and the "
"background color of the entry field changes to light green. If the search "
"pattern does not match any string in the text, this is indicated by a light "
"red background color of the entry field and <guilabel>Not found</guilabel> "
"is displayed at the right side of the bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:918 index.docbook:994
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the <guilabel>Next</guilabel> or <guilabel>Previous</guilabel> button to "
"jump to the next or previous match in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:920
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can modify the search behaviour by selecting different "
"<guilabel>Options</guilabel>: The <guilabel>Highlight all</guilabel> option "
"highlights all matches in the document. Selecting <guilabel>Match case</"
"guilabel> will limit finds to entries that match the case (upper or lower) "
"of each of the characters in the search pattern. The <guilabel>From cursor</"
"guilabel> option begins the search from the current position of the cursor "
"within the document rather than from the beginning."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:928
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the green arrow icon at the right side of the incremental search "
"bar to switch to the power search and replace bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:950
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F3</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Find Next</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:954
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This repeats the last find operation, if any, without calling the "
"incremental search bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:962
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Shift;<keycap>F3</keycap></keycombo> "
"</shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Find Previous</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:971
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This repeats the last find operation, if any, without calling the "
"incremental search bar, and searching backwards instead of forwards through "
"the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:980
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>R</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Replace...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:985
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This command opens the power search and replace bar. On the upper left side "
"of the bar is an icon to close the bar, followed by a small text box for "
"entering the search pattern."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:988
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can control the search mode by selecting <guilabel>Plain Text</"
"guilabel>, <guilabel>Whole Words</guilabel>, <guilabel>Escape Sequences</"
"guilabel> or <guilabel>Regular Expression</guilabel>. For the last two "
"options the <guibutton>Add</guibutton> button is enabled and allows you to "
"add special items to the search pattern from a predefined list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:996
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enter the text to replace with in the text box labeled <guilabel>Replace</"
"guilabel> and click the <guibutton>Replace</guibutton> button to replace "
"only the highlighted text or the <guibutton>Replace All</guibutton> button "
"to replace the search text in the whole document. If the option "
"<guilabel>Use placeholders</guilabel> is checked you can add special items "
"to the replacement text by clicking the <guibutton>Add</guibutton> button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1001
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can modify the search and replace behaviour by selecting different "
"options on the right side of the bar. The <guilabel>Highlight all</guilabel> "
"option highlights all matches in the document. Selecting <guilabel>Match "
"case</guilabel> will limit finds to entries that match the case (upper or "
"lower) of each of the characters in the search pattern. The <guilabel>From "
"cursor</guilabel> option begins the search from the current position of the "
"cursor within the document rather than from the beginning. "
"<guilabel>Selection only</guilabel> will search and replace within the "
"current selection only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1010
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click on the green arrow icon at the right side of the power search and "
"replace bar to switch to the incremental search bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1025
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>H</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Find Selected</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1030
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finds next occurrence of selected text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1036
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>H</keycap></"
"keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu><guimenuitem>Find Selected "
"Backwards</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1041
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finds previous occurrence of selected text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1047
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>G</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Edit</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Go to Line...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1054
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This opens the goto line bar at the bottom of the window which is used to "
"have the cursor jump to a particular line (specified by number) in the "
"document. The line number may be entered directly into the text box or "
"graphically by clicking on the up or down arrow spin controls at the side of "
"the text box. The little up arrow will increase the line number and the down "
"arrow decrease it. Close the bar with a click on the icon on the left side "
"of the bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1069
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>View</guimenu> menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1071
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The <guimenu>View</guimenu> menu allows you to manage settings specific to "
"the active editor, and to manage frames."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1079
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>New Window</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1085
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Create another window containing the current document. All changes to the "
"document in one window are reflected in the other window and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1093
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F7</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Switch to Command Line</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Displays the Katepart command line at the bottom of the window. In the "
"command line, type <userinput>help</userinput> to get help and "
"<userinput>help list</userinput> to get a list of commands."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1110
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Schema</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1116
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select a font schema."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F10</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Dynamic Word Wrap</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1130
#, no-c-format
msgid "The text lines will be wrapped at the view border on the screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F10</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Dynamic Word Wrap Indicators</"
"guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose when and how the dynamic word wrap indicators should be displayed. "
"This is only available if the <guilabel>Dynamic Word Wrap</guilabel> option "
"is checked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1154
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Static Word Wrap Marker</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1160 index.docbook:2214
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, a vertical line will be drawn at the word wrap "
"column as defined in the <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Configure Editor...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> in the Editing "
"tab. Please note that the word wrap marker is only drawn if you use a fixed "
"pitch font."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1172
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F6</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Icon Border</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1179
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a toggle item. Setting it on checked will make the Icon Border "
"visible in the left side of the active editor, and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1187
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F11</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>View</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Line Numbers</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1194
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a toggle Item. Setting it on checked will make a pane displaying the "
"line numbers of the document visible in the left border of the active "
"editor, and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1203
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>View</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Show Scrollbar Marks</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, the view will show marks on the vertical "
"scrollbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1217
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\"><keycap>F9</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenuitem>Show Folding Markers</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1223
#, no-c-format
msgid "If this option is checked, the marks for code folding will be hidden."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guisubmenu
#: index.docbook:1232
#, no-c-format
msgid "Code Folding"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1238
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl; &Shift;<keycap>-</keycap></"
"keycombo></shortcut> <guimenuitem>Collapse Toplevel</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1242
#, no-c-format
msgid "Collapse all toplevel regions in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1245
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl; &Shift;<keycap>+</keycap></"
"keycombo></shortcut> <guimenuitem>Expand Toplevel</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1249
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expand all toplevel regions in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1252
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl; <keycap>-</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenuitem>Collapse One Local Level</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1256
#, no-c-format
msgid "Collapse the region closest to the cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1259
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl; <keycap>+</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenuitem>Expand One Local Level</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1263
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expand the region closest to the cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1286
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1287
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This menu is only displayed, if you check the option <link linkend="
"\"appearance\"> Enable Power User Mode (&kde; 3 mode)</link> on the "
"<guilabel>Appearance</guilabel> page in &kappname;s settings."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1294
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>B</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Set Bookmark</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1303
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets or removes a bookmark in the current line of the active document. (If "
"it's there, it is removed, otherwise one is set)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Clear All Bookmarks</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1318
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This command will remove all the markers from the document as well as the "
"list of markers which is appended at the bottom of this menu item."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1326
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt; <keycap>PgUp</keycap></keycombo></"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu><guimenuitem>Previous</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1330
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will move the cursor to beginning of the first above line with a "
"bookmark. The menuitem text will include the line number and the first piece "
"of text on the line. This item is only available when there is a bookmark in "
"a line above the cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1337
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt; <keycap>PgDown</keycap></"
"keycombo></shortcut> <guimenu>Bookmarks</guimenu><guimenuitem>Next</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1340
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will move the cursor to beginning of the next line with a bookmark. The "
"menuitem text will include the line number and the first piece of text on "
"the line. This item is only available when there is a bookmark in a line "
"below the cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the bottom of this menu, a list of markers appears if any markers are "
"available for this window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1358
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1362
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Read Only Mode</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1366
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Set the current document to Read Only mode. This prevents any text addition "
"and any changes in the document formatting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1372
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Mode</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1376
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the filetype scheme you prefer for the active document. This "
"overwrites the global filetype mode set in <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Editor...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> in the "
"Filetypes tab for your current document only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1386
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Highlighting</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1390
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the Highlighting scheme you prefer for the active document. This "
"overwrites the global highlighting mode set in <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Editor...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> for your current document only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1399
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Indentation</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1403
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose the style of indentation you want for your active document. This "
"overwrites the global indentation mode set in <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Editor...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> for your current document only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1412
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Encoding</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1416
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can overwrite the default encoding set in <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Editor...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> in the <guilabel>Open/Save</guilabel> tab to set a different "
"encoding for your current document. The encoding you set here will be only "
"valid for your current document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1426
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guisubmenu>End of Line</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1430
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose your preferred end of line mode for your active document. This "
"overwrites the global end of line mode set in <menuchoice> "
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Editor...</guimenuitem></"
"menuchoice> for your current document only."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1439
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>Space</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Invoke Code "
"Completion</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1447
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Manually invoke command completion, usually by using a shortcut bound to "
"this action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1452
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Spelling...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1456
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<action>This initiates the spellchecking program - a program designed to "
"help the user catch and correct any spelling errors.</action> Clicking on "
"this entry will start the checker and bring up the speller dialog box "
"through which the user can control the process. There are four settings "
"lined up vertically in the center of the dialog with their corresponding "
"labels just to the left. Starting at the top they are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1465
#, no-c-format
msgid "Unknown word:"
msgstr "Mot desconegut :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1466
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here, the spellchecker indicates the word currently under consideration. "
"This happens when the checker encounters a word not in its dictionary - a "
"file containing a list of correctly spelled words against which it compares "
"each word in the editor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1472
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace with:"
msgstr "Remplaçar per :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1473
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the checker has any similar words in its dictionary the first one will be "
"listed here. The user can accept the suggestion, type in his or her own "
"correction, or choose a different suggestion from the next box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1479
#, no-c-format
msgid "Language:"
msgstr "Lenga :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1480
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you have installed multiple dictionaries, here you can select which "
"dictionary/language should be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1485
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the right side of the dialog box are 6 buttons that allow the user to "
"control the spellcheck process. They are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:1490
#, no-c-format
msgid "Add to Dictionary"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1491
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Pressing this button adds the <guilabel>Unknown word </guilabel> to the "
"checker's dictionary. This means that in the future the checker will always "
"consider this word to be correctly spelled."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1497
#, no-c-format
msgid "Suggest"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1498
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The checker may list here a number of possible replacements for the word "
"under consideration. Clicking on any one of the suggestions will cause that "
"word to be entered in the <guilabel>Replace with</guilabel> box, above."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:1504
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Replace</guibutton>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1505
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button has the checker replace the word under consideration in the "
"document with the word in the <guilabel>Replace with</guilabel> box."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:1510
#, no-c-format
msgid "Replace All"
msgstr "Tot remplaçar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1511
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button causes the checker to replace not only the current "
"<guilabel>Unknown word:</guilabel> but to automatically make the same "
"substitution for any other occurrences of this <guilabel>Unknown word</"
"guilabel> in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:1517
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ignore"
msgstr "Ignorar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1518
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Activating this button will have the checker move on without making any "
"changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:1522
#, no-c-format
msgid "Ignore All"
msgstr "Tot ignorar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1523
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button tells the checker to do nothing with the current "
"<guilabel>Unknown word:</guilabel> and to pass over any other instances of "
"the same word."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1525
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This only applies to the current spellcheck run. If the checker is run again "
"later it will stop on this same word."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1542
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Three more buttons are located horizontally along the bottom of the "
"spellcheck dialog. They are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:1547
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guibutton>Help</guibutton>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1548
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This invokes the &kde; help system starting at the &kappname; help pages "
"(this document)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:1553
#, no-c-format
msgid "Finished"
msgstr "Terminat"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1554
#, no-c-format
msgid "This button ends the spellcheck process, and returns to the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:1559
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cancel"
msgstr "Anullar"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1560
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This button cancels the spellcheck process, all modifications are reverted, "
"and you will return to your document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1570
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Spelling (from cursor)...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1574
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This initiates the spellchecking program but it starts where your cursor is "
"instead of at the beginning of the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1580
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Spellcheck Selection...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1584
#, no-c-format
msgid "Spellchecks the current selection."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1589
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>I</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Indent</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1595
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This increases the paragraph's indentation by one step. The size of the step "
"depends on the <link linkend=\"pref-edit-indent\"> indentation settings</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1602
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>I</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Unindent</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1608
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This reduces the paragraph's indentation by one step. The size of the step "
"depends on the <link linkend=\"pref-edit-indent\"> indentation settings</"
"link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1615
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Clean Indentation</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1618
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This cleans the indentation for the current selection or for the line the "
"cursor is currently in. Cleaning the indentation ensures that all your "
"selected text follows the indentation mode you choose."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1625
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Align</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1630
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Causes a realign of the current line or selected lines using the indentation "
"mode and indentation settings in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1636
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>D</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Comment</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1643
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This adds one space to the beginning of the line where the text cursor is "
"located or to the beginning of any selected lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1650
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>D</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Uncomment</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1657
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This removes one space (if any exist) from the beginning of the line where "
"the text cursor is located or from the beginning of any selected lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1663
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>U</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Uppercase</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1670
#, no-c-format
msgid "Put the selected text or the letter after the cursor in uppercase."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1675
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>U</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Lowercase</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1682
#, no-c-format
msgid "Put the selected text or the letter after the cursor in lowercase."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1687
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Alt;&Ctrl;<keycap>U</keycap></"
"keycombo> </shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Capitalize</"
"guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1694
#, no-c-format
msgid "Capitalize the selected text or the current word."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1699
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>J</keycap></keycombo> </"
"shortcut> <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Join Lines</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1706
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Joins the selected lines, or the current line and the line below with one "
"white space character as a separator. Leading/trailing white space on joined "
"lines is removed in the affected ends."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1712
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Word Wrap Document</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1716
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Apply static word wrapping on all the document. That means that a new line "
"of text will automatically start when the current line exceeds the length "
"specified by the <guilabel>Wrap words at</guilabel> option in the Editing "
"tab in <menuchoice> <guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"Editor...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1725
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Menu items for the selected <link linkend=\"pref-plugins\">plugins</link> "
"are displayed at the end of this menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1739
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1743
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Statusbar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1747
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, this displays a small bar at the bottom of the editor "
"containing information about the status of the current document. When "
"unchecked the status bar is hidden."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1754
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Show Toolbar</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1760
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When checked, this displays a movable toolbar containing buttons used to "
"initiate frequently used commands. When unchecked the toolbar is hidden."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1768
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Path</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1772
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, this displays in the titlebar the path (its location in the "
"file system) of the current document. When unchecked the path is hidden."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1778
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure Editor...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1784
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This menu item opens a dialog whereby several different <link linkend=\"pref-"
"dialog\">settings</link> may be adjusted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1811
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1815
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This command opens a dialog box whereby the <link linkend=\"keybindings"
"\">shortcuts</link> may be changed. A display window shows the list of "
"commands (actions) and their assigned shortcuts, alternates and global "
"shortcuts. The <guilabel>Search</guilabel> line above the list window is "
"used to filter the shortcut list. Selecting an action with a &LMB; click "
"(either on the action name or shortcut cell for the default shortcut or on "
"the alternate cell for an alternative) displays the <guilabel>Default</"
"guilabel> and <guilabel>Custom</guilabel> radio buttons below the selected "
"action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1824
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To assign or change a shortcut click on the <guilabel>None</guilabel> "
"button. Its label changes then to <guilabel>Input</guilabel>, now press the "
"new key combination for the action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1827
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"For example, with the <guilabel>About &kde;</guilabel> action selected in "
"the display window, press the &Ctrl;, &Alt; and the <keycap>K</keycap> key "
"on the keyboard. This would mean that anytime you hold down the &Ctrl; and "
"&Alt; buttons and pressed <keycap>K</keycap> (while using &kappname;) the "
"<guilabel>About &kde;</guilabel> display box would be called."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1832
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use the buttons at the bottom of the dialog to set all shortcuts back to "
"their defaults, print the shortcut list or cancel all changes. Click the "
"<guilabel>OK</guilabel> button to close the dialog and accept all changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: index.docbook:1839
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Toolbars...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1842
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will open the dialog whereby the toolbar configuration may be changed. "
"The user can choose which shortcut buttons should appear on the toolbar. A "
"display window on the left lists the commands available to placed on the "
"toolbar. A display on the right lists those commands already on the toolbar. "
"A set of four arrow buttons between the two displays manipulates the "
"selections. The right pointing arrow places any command selected in the left "
"pane onto the right pane, <abbrev>i.e.</abbrev>, it is added to the toolbar. "
"The left arrow does just the opposite, removing any action selected in the "
"right window from the toolbar. The up and down pointing arrows change the "
"position of an action selected in the right window which changes the "
"position of its button in the toolbar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1859
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Help</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: sect1
#: index.docbook:1859
#, no-c-format
msgid "&help.menu.documentation;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1869
#, no-c-format
msgid "Configure &kappname;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1871
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure "
"Editor...</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menu brings up the "
"<guilabel>Configure Editor</guilabel> dialog box. This dialog can be used to "
"alter a number of different settings. The settings available for change vary "
"according to which category the user chooses from a vertical list on the "
"left side of the dialog. By means of three buttons along the bottom of the "
"box the user can control the process."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1881
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You may invoke the <guilabel>Help</guilabel> system, accept the current "
"settings and close the dialog by means of the <guibutton>OK</guibutton> "
"button, or <guibutton>Cancel</guibutton> the process. The categories "
"<guilabel>Appearance</guilabel>, <guilabel>Fonts &amp; Colors</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Editing</guilabel>, <guilabel>Open/Save</guilabel>, "
"<guilabel>Shortcuts</guilabel> and <guilabel>Extensions</guilabel> are "
"detailed below."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:1892
#, no-c-format
msgid "Appearance"
msgstr "Aparéncia"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1896
#, no-c-format
msgid "Word Wrap"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1900
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dynamic word wrap"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1901
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, the text lines will be wrapped at the view border "
"on the screen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1905
#, no-c-format
msgid "Dynamic word wrap indicators (if applicable)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1906
#, no-c-format
msgid "Choose when the Dynamic word wrap indicators should be displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1910
#, no-c-format
msgid "Align dynamically wrapped lines to indentation depth:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1913
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Enables the start of dynamically wrapped lines to be aligned vertically to "
"the indentation level of the first line. This can help to make code and "
"markup more readable."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1916
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Additionally, this allows you to set a maximum width of the screen, as a "
"percentage, after which dynamically wrapped lines will no longer be "
"vertically aligned. For example, at 50%, lines whose indentation levels are "
"deeper than 50% of the width of the screen will not have vertical alignment "
"applied to subsequent wrapped lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1928
#, no-c-format
msgid "Borders"
msgstr "Bordaduras"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1932
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show folding markers (if available)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1934
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, the current view will display marks for code "
"folding, if code folding is available."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1938
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show icon border"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1940
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is checked, you will see an icon border on the left hand side. The "
"icon border shows bookmark signs for instance."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1944
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show line numbers"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1946
#, no-c-format
msgid "If this is checked, you will see line numbers on the left hand side."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1950
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show scrollbar marks"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1952
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is checked the current view will show marks on the vertical "
"scrollbar. These marks will for instance show bookmarks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1961
#, no-c-format
msgid "Sort Bookmarks Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1963
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"These options are only displayed, if <guilabel>Enable Power User Mode (&kde; "
"3 mode)</guilabel> in the next section is checked."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1968
#, no-c-format
msgid "By position"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1970
#, no-c-format
msgid "The bookmarks will be ordered by the line numbers they are placed at."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1974
#, no-c-format
msgid "By creation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1976
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each new bookmark will be added to the bottom, independently from where it "
"is placed in the document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1984
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Advanced</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1989
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable Power User Mode (&kde; 3 mode)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1991
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Switch between simple and advanced mode. Changing this mode affects only "
"newly opened / created documents. In &kappname; a restart is recommended."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:1996
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show identation lines"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:1998
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is checked, the editor will display vertical lines to help "
"identifying indent lines."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2002
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlight range between selected brackets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2004
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is enabled, the range between the selected matching brackets will be "
"highlighted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2014
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fonts &amp; Colors"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2016
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section of the dialog lets you configure all fonts and colors in any "
"color scheme you have, as well creating new schemes or deleting existing "
"ones. Each scheme has settings for colors, fonts and normal and highlight "
"text styles."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2022
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; will preselect the currently active scheme for you, if you want "
"to work on a different scheme start by selecting that from the "
"<guilabel>Schema</guilabel> combobox. With the <guibutton>New</guibutton> "
"and <guibutton>Delete</guibutton> button you can create a new scheme or "
"delete existing ones."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2026
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"At the bottom of the page you can select the <guilabel>Default schema for "
"&kappname;</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2029
#, no-c-format
msgid "Colors"
msgstr "Colors"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2033
#, no-c-format
