msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Fonts"
msgstr "Poliças"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2111
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can choose the font for the schema. You can choose from any font "
"available on your system, and set a default size. A sample text displays at "
"the bottom of the dialog, so you can see the effect of your choices."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Normal Text Styles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2120
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The normal text styles are inherited by the highlight text styles, allowing "
"the editor to present text in a very consistent way, for example comment "
"text is using the same style in allmost all of the text formats that "
"&kappname; can highlight."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2124 index.docbook:2139
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The name in the list of styles is using the style configured for the item, "
"providing you with an immediate preview when configuring a style."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2127
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each style lets you select common attributes as well as foreground and "
"background colors. To unset a background color, rightclick to use the "
"context menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2133
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlighting Text Styles"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2134
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can edit the text styles used by a specific highlight definition. "
"The editor preselects the highlight used by your current document. To work "
"on a different highlight, select one in the <guilabel>Highlight</guilabel> "
"combobox above the style list."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2142
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Each style lets you select common attributes as well as foreground and "
"background colors. To unset a background color, rightclick to use the "
"context menu. In addition you can see if a style is equal to the default "
"style used for the item, and set it to that if not."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2146
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will notice that many highlights contain other highlights represented by "
"groups in the style list. For example most highlights import the Alert "
"highlight, and many source code formats imports the Doxygen highlight. "
"Editing colors in those groups only affects the styles when used in the "
"edited highlight format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2157
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing"
msgstr "Modificacion"

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2160 index.docbook:2476
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>General</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2164
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tabulators"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2168
#, no-c-format
msgid "Insert spaces instead of tabulators"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2170
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When this is enabled the editor will insert a calculated number of spaces "
"according to the position in the text and the <option>tab-width</option> "
"setting when you press the &Tab; key."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2176
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show tabulators"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2178
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When this is enabled &kappname; will display a small dot as a visual "
"representation of tabulator characters."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2180
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This also causes dots to be drawn to indicate trailing white space. This "
"will be fixed in a future version of &kappname;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2185
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab width"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the <link linkend=\"pref-word-wrap\">Insert spaces instead of tabulators</"
"link> option is selected this entry determines the number of spaces with "
"which the editor will automatically replace tabs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2196
#, no-c-format
msgid "Static Word Wrap"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2197
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Word wrap is a feature that causes the editor to automatically start a new "
"line of text and move (wrap) the cursor to the beginning of that new line. "
"&kappname; will automatically start a new line of text when the current line "
"reaches the length specified by the <link linkend=\"pref-wrap-words-at"
"\">Wrap Words At:</link> option."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2205
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enable static word wrap"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2207
#, no-c-format
msgid "Turns static word wrap on or off."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2211
#, no-c-format
msgid "Show static word wrap markers (if applicable)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2222
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wrap words at:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2224
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If the <link linkend=\"pref-word-wrap\">Enable static word wrap</link> "
"option is selected this entry determines the length (in characters) at which "
"the editor will automatically start a new line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2234
#, no-c-format
msgid "Misc"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2238 index.docbook:2513
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remove trailing spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2239
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kappname; will automatically eliminate extra spaces at the ends of lines of "
"text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2243
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Highlighting"
msgid "Highlight trailing spaces"
msgstr "Enlusiment"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2244
#, no-c-format
msgid "&kappname; will highlight extra spaces at the ends of lines of text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2248
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto brackets"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2248
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the user types a left bracket ([, (, or {) &kappname; automatically "
"enters the right bracket (}, ), or ]) to the right of the cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2260
#, no-c-format
msgid "Cursor &amp; Selection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2265
#, no-c-format
msgid "Text Cursor Movement"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2269
#, no-c-format
msgid "Smart home and smart end"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2271
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When selected, pressing the home key will cause the cursor to skip white "
"space and go to the start of a line's text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2276
#, no-c-format
msgid "Wrap cursor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When on, moving the insertion cursor using the <emphasis role=\"bold\">Left</"
"emphasis> and <emphasis role=\"bold\">Right</emphasis> keys will go on to "
"previous/next line at beginning/end of the line, similar to most editors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2281
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When off, the insertion cursor cannot be moved left of the line start, but "
"it can be moved off the line end, which can be very handy for programmers. "
"When this option is chosen, moving the cursor with the arrow keys off the "
"end of a line (to the right) causes it to jump down to the beginning of the "
"next line. Likewise when the cursor is moved past the beginning of a line "
"(to the left) it jumps up to the end of the preceding line. When this option "
"is not selected, moving the cursor right past the end of a line merely "
"causes it to continue horizontally in the same line and trying to move it "
"left past the beginning does nothing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2293
#, no-c-format
msgid "PageUp/PageDown moves cursor"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2295
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This option changes the behavior of the cursor when the user presses the "
"<keycap>Page Up</keycap> or <keycap>Page Down</keycap> key. If unselected "
"the text cursor will maintain its relative position within the visible text "
"in &kappname; as new text becomes visible as a result of the operation. So "
"if the cursor is in the middle of the visible text when the operation occurs "
"it will remain there (except when one reaches the beginning or end.) With "
"this option selected, the first key press will cause the cursor to move to "
"either the top or bottom of the visible text as a new page of text is "
"displayed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2306
#, no-c-format
msgid "Autocenter cursor (lines):"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2308
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets the number of lines to maintain visible above and below the cursor when "
"possible."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2317
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Selection Mode"
msgid "Text Selection Mode"
msgstr "Mòde de seleccion"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2321
#, no-c-format
msgid "Normal"
msgstr "Normal"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2323
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Selections will be overwritten by typed text and will be lost on cursor "
"movement."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2328
#, no-c-format
msgid "Persistent"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2330
#, no-c-format
msgid "Selections will stay even after cursor movement and typing."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2341
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indentation"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2346
#, no-c-format
msgid "Default Indentation mode:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2348
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Select the automatic indentation mode you want to use as default. It is "
"strongly recommended to use <userinput>None</userinput> or "
"<userinput>Normal</userinput> here, and use filetype configurations to set "
"other indentation modes for text formats like C/C++ code or &XML;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2356
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Properties"
msgid "Indentation Properties"
msgstr "Propietats"

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2360
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indentation width:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2362
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The indentation width is the number of spaces which is used to indent a "
"line. If the option <guilabel>Insert spaces instead of tabulators</guilabel> "
"on the <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab in the <guilabel>Editing</guilabel> "
"page is disabled, a &Tab; character is inserted if the indentation is "
"divisible by the tab width."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2370
#, no-c-format
msgid "Keep Extra Spaces"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2371
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is disabled, changing the indentation level aligns a line to "
"a multiple of the width specified in <guilabel>Indentation width</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2376
#, no-c-format
msgid "Adjust indentation of code pasted from the clipboard"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2378
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, pasted code from the clipboard is indented. "
"Triggering the <guimenuitem>Undo</guimenuitem> action removes the "
"indentation."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2387
#, no-c-format
msgid "Indentation Actions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2391
#, no-c-format
msgid "Backspace key in leading blank space unindents"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2393
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, the <keysym>Backspace</keysym> key decreases the "
"indentation level if the cursor is located in the leading blank space of a "
"line."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2398
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tab key action (if no selection exists)"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2400
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you want &Tab; to align the current line in the current code block like "
"in emacs, make &Tab; a shortcut to the action <guimenuitem>Align</"
"guimenuitem>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2406
#, no-c-format
msgid "Always advance to the next tab position"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2408
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, the &Tab; key always inserts white space so that "
"the next tab position is reached. If the option <guilabel>Insert spaces "
"instead of tabulators</guilabel> on the <guilabel>General</guilabel> tab in "
"the <guilabel>Editing</guilabel> page is enabled, spaces are inserted; "
"otherwise, a single tabulator is inserted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2415
#, no-c-format
msgid "Always increase indentation level"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2417
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, the &Tab; key always indents the current line by "
"the number of character positions specified in <guilabel>Indentation width</"
"guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2423
#, no-c-format
msgid "Increase indentation level if in leading blank space"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2425
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, the &Tab; key either indents the current line or "
"advances to the next tab position. If the insertion point is at or before "
"the first non-space character in the line, or if there is a selection, the "
"current line is indented by the number of character positions specified in "
"<guilabel>Indentation width</guilabel>. If the insertion point is located "
"after the first non-space character in the line and there is no selection, "
"white space is inserted so that the next tab position is reached: if the "
"option <guilabel>Insert spaces instead of tabulators</guilabel> on the "
"<guilabel>General</guilabel> tab in the <guilabel>Editing</guilabel> page is "
"enabled, spaces are inserted; otherwise, a single tabulator is inserted."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2449
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto Completion"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2452
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>General</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2456
#, no-c-format
msgid "Auto Completion enabled"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2458
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If this is enabled, the editor will calculate the number of spaces up to the "
"next tab position as defined by the tab width, and insert that number of "
"spaces instead of a &Tab; character."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2473
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open &amp; Save"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2481
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2485
#, no-c-format
msgid "Encoding:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2487
#, no-c-format
msgid "This sets the default character encoding for your files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2491
#, no-c-format
msgid "End of line:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2493
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Choose your preferred end of line mode for your active document. You have "
"the choice between &UNIX;, DOS/&Windows; or Macintosh."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2498
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic end of line detection"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2500
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Check this if you want the editor to autodetect the end of line type. The "
"first found end of line type will be used for the whole file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2509
#, no-c-format
msgid "Automatic Cleanups on Load/Save"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2515
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The editor will automatically eliminate extra spaces at the ends of lines of "
"text while loading/saving the file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2527
#, no-c-format
msgid "<title>Advanced</title>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2531
#, no-c-format
msgid "Folder Config File"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2535
#, no-c-format
msgid "Search depth for config file:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2537
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The editor will search the given number of folder levels upwards for "
"&kappname; config file and load the settings line from it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2546
#, no-c-format
msgid "Backup on Save"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2547
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Backing up on save will cause &kappname; to copy the disk file to &lt;"
"prefix&gt;&lt;filename&gt;&lt;suffix&gt; before saving changes. The suffix "
"defaults to <emphasis role=\"bold\">~</emphasis> and prefix is empty by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2553
#, no-c-format
msgid "Local files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2555
#, no-c-format
msgid "Check this if you want backups of local files when saving."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2560
#, no-c-format
msgid "Remote files"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2562
#, no-c-format
msgid "Check this if you want backups of remote files when saving."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2566
#, no-c-format
msgid "Prefix"
msgstr "Prefixe"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2568
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the prefix to prepend to the backup file names."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2572
#, no-c-format
msgid "Suffix"
msgstr "Sufixe"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2574
#, no-c-format
msgid "Enter the suffix to add to the backup file names."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2586
#, no-c-format
msgid "Modes &amp; Filetypes"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2587
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This page allows you to override the default configuration for documents of "
"specified mimetypes. When the editor loads a document, it will try if it "
"matches the file masks or mimetypes for one of the defined filetypes, and if "
"so apply the variables defined. If more filetypes match, the one with the "
"highest priority will be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2595
#, no-c-format
msgid "Filetype:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2596 index.docbook:2616
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The filetype with the highest priority is the one displayed in the first "
"drop down box. If more filetypes were found, they are also listed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2601
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>New</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2602
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is used to create a new filetype. After you click on this button, the "
"fields below get empty and you can fill the properties you want for the new "
"filetype."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2607
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guilabel>Delete</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2608
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To remove an existing filetype, select it from the drop down box and press "
"the Delete button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2615
#, no-c-format
msgid "Properties of current filetype"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2621
#, no-c-format
msgid "Name:"
msgstr "Nom :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2622
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The name of the filetype will be the text of the corresponding menu item. "
"This name is displayed in the <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Filetypes</guimenuitem> </menuchoice>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2628
#, no-c-format
msgid "Section:"
msgstr "Seccion :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2629
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The section name is used to organize the file types in menus. This is also "
"used in the <menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu><guimenuitem>Filetypes</"
"guimenuitem> </menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2635
#, no-c-format
msgid "Variables:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2636
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This string allows you to configure &kappname;'s settings for the files "
"selected by this mimetype using &kappname; variables. You can set almost any "
"configuration option, such as highlight, indent-mode, encoding, etc."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2639
#, no-c-format
msgid "For a full list of known variables, see the manual."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2643
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Highlighting"
msgid "Highlighting:"
msgstr "Enlusiment"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2644
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you create a new file type, this drop down box allows you to select a "
"filetype for highlighting."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2648
#, no-c-format
msgid "File extensions:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2649
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The wildcards mask allows you to select files by filename. A typical mask "
"uses an asterisk and the file extension, for example <filename>*.txt; *."
"text</filename>. The string is a semicolon-separated list of masks."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2655
#, no-c-format
msgid "MIME types:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2656
#, no-c-format
msgid "Displays a wizard that helps you easily select mimetypes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guilabel
#: index.docbook:2660
#, no-c-format
msgid "Priority:"
msgstr "Prioritat :"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2661
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Sets a priority for this file type. If more than one file type selects the "
"same file, the one with the highest priority will be used."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: guibutton
#: index.docbook:2668
#, no-c-format
msgid "Download Highlighting Files..."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2670
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click this button to download new or updated syntax highlight descriptions "
"from the &kate; website."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2684
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can change here the shortcut keys configuration. Select an action and "
"click on <guilabel>None</guilabel> next to the <guilabel>Custom</guilabel> "
"radio button and press the key combination, if you want a different shortcut "
"for this action."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2688
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The search line allows you to look for a specific action and see its "
"associated shortcut."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:2693
#, no-c-format
msgid "Extensions"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2694
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This <guilabel>Plugins</guilabel> tab lists all available plugins and you "
"can check those you want to use. Click on the <guibutton>Information</"
"guibutton> button to open the <guilabel>About</guilabel> dialog of this "
"plugin. Once a plugin is checked, the <guibutton>Configure</guibutton> "
"button is enabled and you can click it in order to configure the highlighted "
"plugin."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:2701
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The selected plugins are available in the <guimenu>Tools</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

